course: dictionary
lesson: 1135
title: Breed: a kind of animal, and to have young
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Breed is a word with two jobs. As a noun, a breed is a particular kind of dog, cat, horse or farm animal, like a Labrador or a poodle. As a verb, to breed means for animals to have babies, or for people to keep animals so they have young.
explain: Use the context to decide which job the word is doing. «In Siberia scientists bred only the tamest foxes for over 60 years.» Here bred is a verb: the scientists kept the foxes so they had young, and they chose the friendliest ones. Check it by swapping in «had babies»: the sentence still makes sense.
explain: Look for the clues around the word. «Farm sheep... people bred them to keep their wool» tells you that people chose sheep to have young because of their wool. Bred is the past tense of breed, so it means they did it in the past. Breed, bred and breeding are all forms of the same word.
fact: Breed can be a noun (a breed) or a verb (to breed).
fact: A breed is a particular kind of dog, cat, horse or farm animal, like a Labrador or a poodle.
fact: The past tense of breed is bred, as in «In Siberia scientists bred only the tamest foxes.»
fact: To breed means for animals to have young, as in «Birds breed in spring.»
fact: Breeding season is the time of year when animals have their young.
exercise: «In Siberia scientists bred only the tamest foxes for over 60 years.» What does bred mean here? | Sold the animals at the market | Ran away from the zoo | Cooked food for the animals | *Kept animals so they had young, choosing the friendliest
exercise: Which meaning fits in «A poodle is a breed of dog»? | To run fast | To have babies | *A particular kind of dog | To cook food
exercise: Find and copy one word from «Farm sheep grow wool all the time and must be shorn every year, because people bred them to keep their wool» that is a past form of breed. | every | *bred | grow | wool
test: «Zoos breed it in very clean rooms and release eggs and young frogs into the mountains.» What does breed mean here? | *To keep animals so they have young | To sell tickets to visitors | To fight with other frogs | To clean the rooms
test: «Birds breed in spring.» Which word could replace breed without changing the meaning? | Hide | Sleep | *Have babies | Migrate away
exam: Ravi says a breed is only ever a kind of dog. What does the dictionary say? | A breed is a kind of bird's nest | Ravi is right, because a breed is always a dog | *Breed can also mean a kind of cat, horse or farm animal, so Ravi is wrong | A breed is a sound an animal makes
